{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Paq7xU8aiaiQDYZaFsn8ez","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So two divergences: `seq 0.8 0.1 1.2` and `seq 0.1 0.1 0.3`.\n\nFor `seq 0.1 0.1 0.3`:\n- i=2: val = 0.1 + 2*0.1 = 0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004\n- Since 0.30000000000000004 > 0.3, `inRange` returns false, and we don't print 0.3.\n\n\n- But gseq prints 0.3 because long double accumulation has less error, so the root cause is floating-point tolerance in the inRange function. I need to add tolerance proportional to the step size to handle the accumulation error difference between float64 and long double.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1736,"cache_read_input_tokens":48474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1736},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b75f48fa-b318-4f07-9709-f5ff65656f95","uuid":"2f38153f-c163-4e84-8b0f-93aab3b22c5c"}
