{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DzJg4GwRvkzVQPTXdjspyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Changes are clean. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**main.go** — Two fixes for floating-point edge cases:\n\n1. **`inRange` tolerance** (line 344-350): Changed from strict `val <= last` to `val - last <= eps` where `eps = |incr| * 1e-10`. This compensates for float64 accumulation error that causes values to slightly overshoot the endpoint (GNU seq avoids this by using 80-bit long double).\n\n2. **Duplicate detection** (line 309, 312-314, 323): Added `prev` tracking to break when `val == prev`, preventing duplicate output when precision is exhausted near 2^53.\n\n**seq_test.go** — Five new differential test cases:\n- `float-accum-0.8-0.1-1.2` — float accumulation that previously missed the endpoint\n- `float-accum-0.1-0.1-0.3` — same class of bug with different values\n- `descending-float-1.0-neg0.1-0.0` — descending float coverage\n- `equal-width-neg5-5` — equal-width with negative range\n- `first-equals-last` — R1.3 edge case (FIRST == LAST)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":743,"cache_read_input_tokens":56724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":743},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b75f48fa-b318-4f07-9709-f5ff65656f95","uuid":"477a2ce2-440a-4929-a869-822d68498353"}
